WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.703
Harry Kersh: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:05.205
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:07.774
between Taco Bell in the US and the UK.

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:09.242
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.314
Joe Avella: Taco Bell.

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:15.448
We're talking tacos.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:16.383
At the US Taco Bell,

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:19.486
you can get an individual hard-shell taco,

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:23.056
or you can get three

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:25.191
with a drink. I went with medium.

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:28.695
Or you can get a party pack, which is 12.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:31.164
Yeah, get a load of this.

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:35.468
It's like I'm presenting
a newborn. [laughs]

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:36.736
Aw.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.905
Harry: The serving sizes
for tacos in the UK

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:40.607
are one individual taco,

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:41.441
or...

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:48.214
two tacos, fries, and a
drink, which is a combo meal.

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:50.517
Joe: This is a US beef taco supreme.

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.619
First thing I'm gonna do is measure it.

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:53.720
Hang on. Oh, man.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.523
It's almost exactly 6 inches.

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:57.490
All right.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.359
Let's weigh it.

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.061
New scale!

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:03.263
Doo doo doo doo doo doo
doo doo doo, what is it?

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:04.531
Oh, we're over 100 grams.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:07.767
Harry: This is a crunchy
beef taco supreme in the UK.

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:11.538
It measures exactly 5 inches across,

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:14.107
and it weighs 70 grams.

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:17.544
Joe: Wow. That's way heavier.

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:18.645
What is up?

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.480
Harry: This is a standard burrito in the UK.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.848
We've gone for crispy chicken.

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.483
Joe: I also went with chicken.

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:26.719
Harry: It measures 6 1/2 inches in length.

00:01:26.719 --> 00:01:28.321
Joe: Oh, you know what?

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:29.289
6 1/2 inches.

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:30.323
Harry: And it weighs...

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:36.696
about 210 grams.

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:37.997
Joe: 230.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:39.365
Here's our quesadilla.

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:40.934
It is...

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.535
yo, dude, it's a foot!

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:43.803
12 inches!

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:46.005
Harry: This is a UK chicken quesadilla.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:48.575
It measures 10 inches in length,

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:50.009
and it weighs...

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:54.481
245 grams.

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.216
Joe: Yeah, about 245.

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:58.318
Weighs the same. Wider.

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:02.455
Harry: ♪ Crunchwrap Supreme ♪

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.625
This is a Crunchwrap Supreme in the UK.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:08.628
It measures 6 inches point to point,

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:09.963
and it weighs...

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.434
about 240 grams.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:15.768
Joe: What's six sides?

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:17.170
Without looking it up,

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.939
does anyone know what
a six-sided shape is?

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.641
Hey, Siri.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.843
What is a six-sided shape?

00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:26.579
Siri: According to Giantbomb.com,

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:28.481
regular hexagons are six-sided.

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:30.016
Joe: Hexagons!

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:33.486
Yo, dude, guess how many inches.

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:38.191
6, baby.

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:40.026
That is, obviously, that's on purpose.

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:44.597
I wonder if there is something
about six sides, 6 inches.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:46.099
[spooky music]

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:48.768
If this thing weighs 666 grams,

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.436
I will never not eat these.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:51.838
Here we go.

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:59.746
275 for the hexagon Crunchwrap Supreme.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.949
Six sides, 6 inches.

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:05.051
Harry: What's the biggest
thing on the UK menu?

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:08.588
Well, for us, it's the
Classic Cravings Meal for six.

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:11.824
Joe: In the US, biggest thing on the menu,

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:13.359
remember this guy?

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:14.594
Taco party pack.

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:15.995
Harry: The Classic Cravings Meal for six

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:18.431
comes with two quesadillas,

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:22.402
two beef Crunchwrap Supremes,
two Volcano burritos,

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:25.271
two portions of nachos BellGrande,

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:27.040
and then six beef tacos

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:30.143
and three portions of
cinnamon twists for dessert.

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:31.711
Joe: As you can see, it's just 12 tacos.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.746
I know that seems very
simple, but sometimes,

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:35.915
simplicity is the best.

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.784
12 tacos, you can get them either

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:39.419
hard shell or soft shell,

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:41.654
regular or supreme, at least half of them

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.856
I know you can get as Doritos Tacos Locos.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:44.691
If you don't know what that is,

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:46.326
you'll find out a little
bit later here in the US.

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:49.762
Harry: Let's take a look at some of the

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.064
nutritional info for Taco Bell,

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:52.465
starting with the basics.

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:55.468
In the UK, a plain crunchy beef taco

00:03:55.468 --> 00:04:00.006
is 159 calories and has
308 milligrams of sodium.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.609
Joe: In the US, our crunchy beef taco

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:04.877
is 170 calories.

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:06.646
Harry: A chicken quesadilla in the UK

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:08.681
is a hefty 529 calories.

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:11.150
Joe: Our quesadilla
actually has less calories.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.919
"Only" 510.

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:14.687
But it still has more sodium.

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:16.756
It actually has almost more than half

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:17.890
of your daily allowance.

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:19.259
Harry: Thud.

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:22.629
While in the UK, a Crunchwrap has 578 calories,

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:24.297
but shockingly, it has 60%

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:26.065
of your daily saturated fat allowance.

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:29.502
Joe: In the US, our hexagram is 530 calories

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:32.972
and has about 6 grams of fat
less than the one in the UK.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:36.676
But, surprising no one, ours has more sodium.

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:38.344
As is always the case in the US,

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:39.712
you have to look at the beverages.

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:42.849
This right here is a large Mountain Dew Baja Blast.

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:45.518
This is 30 ounces of a liquid

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:47.754
that is the most unnatural green I've ever seen.

00:04:47.754 --> 00:04:48.655
It glows in the dark.

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:50.957
It's so bright, when I close
my eyes I can still see it,

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.158
like when you look at the sun.

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:57.063
This beverage has over 420 calories.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.432
That is ridiculous. I gotta take a sip.

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.036
Oh, my God.

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:07.640
This has roughly 110 grams of sugar.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.409
It's an absurd amount of sugar.

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:12.278
Oh, God. It's like, it's horrible,

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:13.546
yet I'm addicted to it.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:16.582
So, I wanted to see exactly what

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:19.319
110 grams of sugar looks like.

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:21.421
And to do so...

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:22.588
get out of my face.

00:05:22.822 --> 00:05:27.293
We got this and this.

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:32.699
Come on, are you serious?

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:33.766
I'm not even halfway there.

00:05:37.704 --> 00:05:38.905
Yeah, OK, there we go.

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:41.708
This is in that.

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:45.812
America, this is too much sugar.

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:46.412
I get it.

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:49.349
This thing, it's just....

00:05:51.317 --> 00:05:52.518
Ah.

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:53.786
Man!

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:56.389
I hate that so much.

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:00.827
Harry: Let's start with the
ingredients for the basics.

00:06:00.827 --> 00:06:03.763
In the UK, a flour tortilla
contains the following.

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:04.997
Fortified wheat flour,

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:07.066
made with wheat flour, calcium carbonate,

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:09.302
iron, niacin, and thiamin;

00:06:09.302 --> 00:06:10.269
[fast-forwarding] water; vegetable oils,

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:11.404
which are palm oil and rapeseed oil;

00:06:11.404 --> 00:06:13.639
raising agents E500, E450, and E296;

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:15.641
sugar; emulsifier E471; salt;

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:18.010
[normal speed] and a flour
treatment agent, E920.

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:20.346
Joe: [blubbering]

00:06:20.346 --> 00:06:21.614
Here we go.

00:06:21.614 --> 00:06:23.316
In the US, our flour tortillas

00:06:23.316 --> 00:06:25.651
have enriched wheat flour; water;

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:27.220
vegetable shortening, which is soybean,

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:30.089
hydrogenated soybean,
and/or cottonseed oil;

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:31.257
[fast-forwarding] sugar; salt;
leavening — baking soda,

00:06:31.257 --> 00:06:33.192
sodium acid pyrophosphate; molasses;

00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:34.660
dough conditioner, which is fumaric acid,

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:36.963
distilled monoglycerides? Yeah.
Enzymes, vital wheat gluten,

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:39.031
cellulose gum, wheat starch,
calcium carbonate; calcium;

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:41.501
[normal speed] pra-po-nee-ate.
Pra-po-nee-ate.

00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:44.470
Pro-po-nate. Proponate. Propionate.

00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:45.605
That's a tough one.

00:06:45.605 --> 00:06:49.642
Sorbic acid and/or potassium sorbate.

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:51.377
Harry: These lists might
look quite different,

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:53.679
but actually a lot of it's
just under terminology.

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:56.416
For example, the UK menu
tends to use E numbers,

00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:58.351
whereas the US menu tends to refer

00:06:58.351 --> 00:07:00.186
to things by their full chemical names.

00:07:00.286 --> 00:07:02.221
Joe: Yeah, it's a good
distinction to make, Harry,

00:07:02.221 --> 00:07:03.723
but is it better? I don't know.

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:06.859
What sounds worse, E450 or pyrophosphate?

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:09.195
Pyrophosphate is a
scary-sounding chemical.

00:07:09.195 --> 00:07:11.264
E450 sounds like a "Star Wars" droid.

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:12.532
I don't think it really makes

00:07:12.532 --> 00:07:13.699
much of a difference, personally.

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:15.334
Harry: What about some meat options?

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:19.138
Well, in the UK, 72% of the beef is beef,

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:21.908
and the rest is made up of beef fat,

00:07:21.908 --> 00:07:25.178
maltodextrin, tomato
powder, paprika, cumin,

00:07:25.178 --> 00:07:28.981
black pepper, salt, chili
powder, garlic powder,

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:32.785
onion powder, yeast extract,
oregano, cocoa powder,

00:07:32.785 --> 00:07:36.722
flavor enhancer E635, cellulose, salt,

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:39.759
stabilizers E451 and E452.

00:07:39.926 --> 00:07:41.394
Joe: And in the United States,

00:07:41.394 --> 00:07:43.529
our beef contains beef.

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:44.630
Imagine that.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:48.201
Water, seasoning, which is
cellulose, chili pepper,

00:07:48.201 --> 00:07:52.305
maltodextrin, salt, oats,
soy lecithin, spices,

00:07:52.305 --> 00:07:55.441
tomato powder, sugar,
onion powder, citric acid,

00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:57.310
natural flavors, new set of brackets,

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:59.512
(including smoke flavor),
close them brackets,

00:07:59.512 --> 00:08:04.383
torula yeast, cocoa, disodium inosinate,

00:08:04.383 --> 00:08:05.284
and

00:08:05.284 --> 00:08:06.018
[sighs]

00:08:06.185 --> 00:08:07.053
what is this word?

00:08:12.892 --> 00:08:13.826
Whatever.

00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:15.862
It looks like it's pretty
much the same thing

00:08:15.862 --> 00:08:16.896
you guys got there in the UK.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:20.399
One thing we need to note
about the US Taco Bell menu

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:22.168
is that items like the Baja Blast

00:08:22.168 --> 00:08:24.003
and the Doritos Tacos Locos,

00:08:24.003 --> 00:08:26.172
I think the shells have an ingredient

00:08:26.172 --> 00:08:28.407
called Yellow No. 5.

00:08:28.407 --> 00:08:30.543
Yellow No. 5 is not in the UK.

00:08:30.543 --> 00:08:31.711
Of course it's in the US.

00:08:31.911 --> 00:08:33.946
Harry: In the UK, you
usually find Yellow 5

00:08:33.946 --> 00:08:35.681
referred to as tartrazine.

00:08:35.681 --> 00:08:37.884
It's on a list of six chemicals

00:08:37.884 --> 00:08:39.085
which, when added to food,

00:08:39.085 --> 00:08:40.887
must contain the following warning:

00:08:40.887 --> 00:08:42.822
"May have an adverse effect on activity

00:08:42.822 --> 00:08:44.323
and attention in children."

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:50.029
Joe: And according to
the FDA, in some cases,

00:08:50.029 --> 00:08:53.299
it causes itching and
hives in people who eat it.

00:08:53.299 --> 00:08:54.700
Disgusting.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:55.935
[laughs]

00:08:55.935 --> 00:08:58.771
Itching and hives, yep, that's fine.

00:08:58.771 --> 00:09:01.507
Hey, I ate it growing up,
and I'm perfectly fine.

00:09:01.507 --> 00:09:02.842
I should note that I have a full head

00:09:02.842 --> 00:09:04.544
of gray hair, and I just turned 23.

00:09:06.979 --> 00:09:08.147
Harry: Here is everything
you can only find

00:09:08.147 --> 00:09:09.782
on the menu at a UK Taco Bell.

00:09:10.049 --> 00:09:12.885
Joe: This is everything you could only get

00:09:12.885 --> 00:09:14.220
at a US Taco Bell.

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:16.822
Harry: So, we only have
the one exclusive taco.

00:09:16.822 --> 00:09:18.057
And it's this one,

00:09:18.057 --> 00:09:21.160
which is the crispy chicken soft taco.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:23.696
What it is, is pretty
much just a standard taco

00:09:23.696 --> 00:09:26.032
with the lettuce, the
cheese, the sour cream,

00:09:26.032 --> 00:09:27.366
but then we've kind of
got one of these breaded

00:09:27.366 --> 00:09:29.001
crispy chicken fillets
in the middle as well.

00:09:29.235 --> 00:09:30.469
Joe: First thing, which
is right in front of me,

00:09:30.469 --> 00:09:31.804
I've talked about this twice already.

00:09:31.804 --> 00:09:32.905
It is the party pack.

00:09:33.306 --> 00:09:35.074
We've already met the Baja Blast.

00:09:37.276 --> 00:09:39.145
Oh, man, I hate it so much.

00:09:39.245 --> 00:09:42.281
One thing that I love at Taco Bell,

00:09:42.281 --> 00:09:45.952
the Doritos Locos tacos. What is it?

00:09:45.952 --> 00:09:50.957
It is a taco that the shell is a Dorito.

00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:52.224
See that?

00:09:52.224 --> 00:09:53.125
Made of the same stuff.

00:09:53.426 --> 00:09:54.293
Harry: Now, we actually have a bunch

00:09:54.293 --> 00:09:56.629
of exclusive burrito options in the UK.

00:09:56.629 --> 00:09:59.432
We'll start with this one,
which is the Volcano burrito.

00:09:59.432 --> 00:10:01.367
Now, apparently this used
to be on the menu in the US,

00:10:01.367 --> 00:10:02.735
but it's no longer there.

00:10:02.735 --> 00:10:04.103
What it is, is basically just, like,

00:10:04.103 --> 00:10:05.871
a beef and rice burrito.

00:10:05.871 --> 00:10:07.940
There's some sour cream
cheese in there as well

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:09.575
and some crunchy tortilla chips.

00:10:09.575 --> 00:10:11.077
And I think it gets the name Volcano

00:10:11.077 --> 00:10:12.545
because it's got the lava sauce in there,

00:10:12.545 --> 00:10:13.879
so it's quite spicy.

00:10:14.380 --> 00:10:16.282
Joe: Yes, Harry, the Volcano
burrito was available

00:10:16.282 --> 00:10:18.451
in the US for a limited time.

00:10:18.451 --> 00:10:20.653
It was a promotional menu item

00:10:20.653 --> 00:10:25.458
for the 1995 box-office bomb "Congo,"

00:10:25.458 --> 00:10:27.126
based on the Michael Crichton book.

00:10:27.126 --> 00:10:28.794
RIP to my boy Michael Crichton.

00:10:28.928 --> 00:10:31.030
Harry: Here, we have
a beefy nacho griller,

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:32.765
which is a fantastic name.

00:10:32.765 --> 00:10:35.701
What this is, is just beef
and crushed nacho chips

00:10:35.701 --> 00:10:37.870
with some cheese sauce in a burrito.

00:10:38.270 --> 00:10:41.440
Here, we've got the double
cheesy black bean burrito,

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:43.709
which, as the name suggests,
has two types of cheese.

00:10:43.709 --> 00:10:45.044
It's got the nacho cheese

00:10:45.044 --> 00:10:46.479
and also the shredded cheese in there,

00:10:46.479 --> 00:10:48.614
as well as some rice and black beans.

00:10:48.814 --> 00:10:50.716
Here, we have the seven-layer burrito.

00:10:50.883 --> 00:10:52.885
We have another exclusive
crispy chicken option,

00:10:52.885 --> 00:10:54.920
which is a crispy chicken burrito.

00:10:55.087 --> 00:10:57.323
And then, finally, we have
the spicy chicken griller.

00:10:59.859 --> 00:11:00.860
Not bad.

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:01.827
It does just kind of taste like

00:11:01.827 --> 00:11:03.896
something that I could make at home.

00:11:03.896 --> 00:11:05.364
Joe: There's a bunch of burritos.

00:11:05.364 --> 00:11:07.466
I'm gonna try and figure
out what these burritos are

00:11:07.466 --> 00:11:09.268
without, like, completely
ripping them apart.

00:11:09.268 --> 00:11:10.102
This right here.

00:11:11.003 --> 00:11:12.805
Oh, beef Quesarito.

00:11:12.805 --> 00:11:15.307
Somehow they combined a
burrito and a quesadilla,

00:11:15.307 --> 00:11:18.778
and it's this light-brown brick.

00:11:18.878 --> 00:11:20.946
If you don't want beef,
you wanna go vegetarian,

00:11:20.946 --> 00:11:23.816
they also have a black bean Quesarito.

00:11:24.116 --> 00:11:26.485
This looks like five-layer burrito.

00:11:26.485 --> 00:11:28.054
I didn't know this until
I had to do this video,

00:11:28.054 --> 00:11:29.989
but there's no seven-layer
burrito in America anymore.

00:11:30.122 --> 00:11:33.292
They took out two layers,
and I get the five-layer one.

00:11:33.492 --> 00:11:36.195
[grunts] What is this?

00:11:36.462 --> 00:11:38.397
Well, all these just look the same.

00:11:39.031 --> 00:11:40.199
Grilled cheese burrito.

00:11:41.767 --> 00:11:42.835
That sounds awesome.

00:11:42.835 --> 00:11:44.236
Who doesn't like grilled cheese?

00:11:44.303 --> 00:11:46.806
And these two that are left here,

00:11:46.806 --> 00:11:51.811
one of them is a cheesy
bean and rice burrito,

00:11:51.811 --> 00:11:53.779
and the other one is a burrito supreme.

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:56.148
That's one of these two.

00:11:56.148 --> 00:11:57.283
I don't know which is which.

00:11:57.283 --> 00:11:58.951
We also have steak quesadillas,

00:11:58.951 --> 00:12:00.386
which, unfortunately the Taco Bell

00:12:00.386 --> 00:12:01.454
that I went to did not have them.

00:12:01.587 --> 00:12:02.855
This big thing right here,

00:12:02.855 --> 00:12:04.223
I love this. Look at this.

00:12:04.223 --> 00:12:06.559
This is the nacho party pack.

00:12:06.559 --> 00:12:07.827
It's exactly what it sounds like.

00:12:07.827 --> 00:12:09.061
Get a good look, UK.

00:12:09.061 --> 00:12:10.796
This is what nachos are
supposed to look like.

00:12:10.996 --> 00:12:12.298
Harry: What we lack in nachos,

00:12:12.298 --> 00:12:14.333
we more than make up for in fries.

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:15.768
We love fries in the UK.

00:12:15.768 --> 00:12:17.002
Obviously, we call them chips.

00:12:17.069 --> 00:12:19.538
But it's very unusual to walk
into a fast-food restaurant

00:12:19.538 --> 00:12:20.706
and not be able to find them,

00:12:20.706 --> 00:12:22.041
so I think Taco Bell have kind of tried

00:12:22.041 --> 00:12:23.342
to cash in on that in the UK.

00:12:23.442 --> 00:12:25.244
Basically your standard
fries, but then they have

00:12:25.244 --> 00:12:27.079
a kind of fajita
seasoning on them as well.

00:12:27.446 --> 00:12:29.148
You can get them in three sizes.

00:12:29.148 --> 00:12:30.049
Regular fries,

00:12:30.049 --> 00:12:32.118
then you have the fries supreme,

00:12:32.118 --> 00:12:34.887
and then finally you have the fries BellGrande,

00:12:34.887 --> 00:12:36.155
which is the biggest size.

00:12:36.188 --> 00:12:38.357
We ordered one deconstructed

00:12:38.357 --> 00:12:40.726
and one constructed just
to see the difference.

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:43.496
Joe: Mexican pizza.

00:12:43.496 --> 00:12:44.396
They were saying for a while

00:12:44.396 --> 00:12:46.398
that these were gonna
be taken off the menu.

00:12:47.266 --> 00:12:49.502
We still got them in a
couple locations, apparently.

00:12:49.502 --> 00:12:50.703
I got my hands on one.

00:12:50.703 --> 00:12:51.670
Look at this guy.

00:12:53.105 --> 00:12:56.509
Oh, this right here, the
power bowl, the protein bowl.

00:12:56.509 --> 00:12:59.445
This is actually a really
good idea for them.

00:12:59.445 --> 00:13:01.680
It's just all protein, no carbs.

00:13:01.781 --> 00:13:03.749
Harry: Now, the only side
that seems to be exclusive

00:13:03.749 --> 00:13:06.252
to the UK is actually just
a little bowl of rice.

00:13:06.252 --> 00:13:08.220
For some reason, I couldn't
find this on the US menu.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:09.588
If I was wrong, let me know.

00:13:09.889 --> 00:13:13.359
Joe: What everyone in the UK

00:13:13.359 --> 00:13:16.228
has been waiting for!
[drumroll]

00:13:16.228 --> 00:13:19.899
Taco Bell breakfast, yes!

00:13:19.899 --> 00:13:23.969
I think, of all the
fast-food breakfasts-es,

00:13:23.969 --> 00:13:26.305
Taco Bell's is the best.

00:13:26.305 --> 00:13:29.008
These are the items that
you can get here in America,

00:13:29.008 --> 00:13:30.843
and they are all great.

00:13:30.843 --> 00:13:33.546
The cheesy toasted breakfast burrito.

00:13:34.713 --> 00:13:37.550
The hash brown toasted burrito.

00:13:38.484 --> 00:13:41.620
The grande toasted breakfast burrito.

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:43.022
Another one I wanna point out here

00:13:43.022 --> 00:13:46.091
is the breakfast Crunchwrap Supreme.

00:13:46.091 --> 00:13:48.227
Of course, we all know this shape.

00:13:49.428 --> 00:13:50.529
Hexagon?

00:13:50.629 --> 00:13:52.932
They're like the regular burritos

00:13:52.932 --> 00:13:54.400
you would get at Taco Bell,

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:55.501
but they have eggs in them.

00:13:55.501 --> 00:13:57.937
Sometimes they have
bacon, a pico de gallo.

00:13:57.937 --> 00:14:00.206
They're all very good. Very, very good.

00:14:00.272 --> 00:14:01.207
Harry: I'm really sad that we don't have

00:14:01.207 --> 00:14:03.142
any breakfast items in the UK,

00:14:03.142 --> 00:14:05.945
but what we do have is
churros for dessert.

00:14:08.614 --> 00:14:10.649
These can be served with a little pot of

00:14:10.649 --> 00:14:12.885
dulce de leche to dip in.

00:14:12.885 --> 00:14:15.120
And, honestly, I'm shocked
that you guys don't have these.

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:19.124
[crunching]

00:14:20.025 --> 00:14:21.727
Joe: For the US Taco Bell desserts,

00:14:21.727 --> 00:14:23.829
the one thing we got here
you can't get in the UK

00:14:23.829 --> 00:14:26.432
are these Cinnabon Delights.

00:14:26.665 --> 00:14:27.833
They're like little cinnamon balls.

00:14:27.833 --> 00:14:30.669
You can get them in either an order of two

00:14:30.669 --> 00:14:32.738
or 12 or any number in between.

00:14:34.874 --> 00:14:35.841
Oh, my God.

00:14:36.709 --> 00:14:38.711
There's cream inside of these.
I was not expecting that.

00:14:38.978 --> 00:14:40.546
Exclusive drinks in the US.

00:14:40.546 --> 00:14:42.648
This one is a dragon fruit freeze.

00:14:42.648 --> 00:14:45.184
That was like a Slurpee.

00:14:45.184 --> 00:14:46.318
You can also get Powerade.

00:14:46.318 --> 00:14:48.687
They got fruit punch Powerade on tap.

00:14:48.721 --> 00:14:50.489
Right here, pink lemonade.

00:14:50.489 --> 00:14:52.524
And for the

00:14:52.524 --> 00:14:53.459
[laughs]

00:14:53.459 --> 00:14:55.694
Baja Blast frie-- ah, fiends,

00:14:55.694 --> 00:14:59.265
they also have a Baja Blast freeze.

00:15:00.165 --> 00:15:01.967
Yuck.

00:15:02.268 --> 00:15:05.204
In the US, our Taco Bell also has

00:15:05.204 --> 00:15:07.072
iced coffee and iced tea.

